sodium.options.pages.quality=Quality
sodium.options.pages.performance=Performance
sodium.options.pages.advanced=Advanced
sodium.options.view_distance.tooltip=The render distance controls how far away terrain will be rendered. Shorter distances mean that less terrain will be rendered, improving frame rates.
sodium.options.simulation_distance.tooltip=The simulation distance controls how far away terrain and entities will be loaded and ticked. Shorter distances can reduce the internal server's load and may improve frame rates.
sodium.options.brightness.tooltip=Controls the brightness (gamma) of the game.
sodium.options.clouds.name=Clouds
sodium.options.clouds.tooltip=Controls whether or not clouds will be visible.
sodium.options.gui_scale.tooltip=Sets the maximum scale factor to be used for the user interface. If 'auto' is used, then the largest scale factor will always be used.
sodium.options.fullscreen.tooltip=If enabled, the game will display in full-screen (if supported).
sodium.options.v_sync.tooltip=If enabled, the game's frame rate will be synchronized to the monitor's refresh rate, making for a generally smoother experience at the expense of overall input latency. This setting might reduce performance if your system is too slow.
sodium.options.fps_limit.tooltip=Limits the maximum number of frames per second. This can help reduce battery usage and general system load when multi-tasking. If V-Sync is enabled, this option will be ignored unless it is lower than your display's refresh rate.
sodium.options.view_bobbing.tooltip=If enabled, the player's view will sway and bob when moving around. Players who experience motion sickness while playing can benefit from disabling this.
sodium.options.attack_indicator.tooltip=Controls where the Attack Indicator is displayed on screen.
sodium.options.autosave_indicator.tooltip=If enabled, an indicator will be shown when the game is saving the world to disk.
sodium.options.graphics_quality.tooltip=The default graphics quality controls some legacy options and is necessary for mod compatibility. If the options below are left to \"Default\ they will use this setting.
sodium.options.clouds_quality.tooltip=Controls the quality of rendered clouds in the sky.
sodium.options.weather_quality.tooltip=Controls the quality of rain and snow effects.
sodium.options.leaves_quality.name=Leaves Quality
sodium.options.leaves_quality.tooltip=Controls the quality of leaves. Fast culls the hidden faces between adjacent leaf blocks while keeping the fancy leaf texture, greatly reducing geometry in forests.
sodium.options.particle_quality.name=Particle Quality
sodium.options.particle_quality.tooltip=Controls the maximum number of particles which can be present on screen at any one time.
sodium.options.smooth_lighting.tooltip=Controls whether blocks will be smoothly lit and shaded. This slightly increases the amount of time needed to re-build a chunk, but doesn't affect frame rates.
sodium.options.biome_blend.name=Biome Blend
sodium.options.biome_blend.value=%s block(s)
sodium.options.biome_blend.tooltip=Controls the range which biomes will be sampled for block colorization. Higher values greatly increase the amount of time it takes to build chunks for diminishing improvements in quality.
sodium.options.entity_distance.name=Entity Distance
sodium.options.entity_distance.tooltip=Controls how far away entities can render from the player. Higher values increase the render distance at the expense of frame rates.
sodium.options.entity_shadows.tooltip=If enabled, basic shadows will be rendered beneath mobs and other entities.
sodium.options.vignette.name=Vignette
sodium.options.vignette.tooltip=If enabled, a vignette effect will be rendered on the player's view. This is very unlikely to make a difference to frame rates unless you are fill-rate limited.
sodium.options.mipmap_levels.tooltip=Controls the number of mipmaps which will be used for block model textures. Higher values provide better rendering of blocks in the distance, but may adversely affect performance with many animated textures.
sodium.options.use_chunk_multidraw.name=Use Chunk Multi-Draw
sodium.options.use_chunk_multidraw.tooltip=Multi-draw allows multiple chunks to be rendered with fewer draw calls, greatly reducing CPU overhead when rendering the world while also potentially allowing for more efficient GPU utilization. This optimization may cause issues with some graphics drivers, so you should try disabling it if you are experiencing glitches.
sodium.options.use_vertex_objects.name=Use Vertex Array Objects
sodium.options.use_vertex_objects.tooltip=Helps to improve performance by moving information about how vertex data should be rendered into the driver, allowing it to better optimize for repeated rendering of the same objects. There is generally no reason to disable this unless you're using incompatible mods.
sodium.options.use_block_face_culling.name=Use Block Face Culling
sodium.options.use_block_face_culling.tooltip=If enabled, only the sides of blocks which are facing the camera will be submitted for rendering. This can eliminate a large number of block faces very early in the rendering process, saving memory bandwidth and time on the GPU. Some resource packs may have issues with this option, so try disabling it if you're seeing holes in blocks.
sodium.options.use_compact_vertex_format.name=Use Compact Vertex Format
sodium.options.use_compact_vertex_format.tooltip=If enabled, a more compact vertex format will be used for rendering chunks. This can reduce graphics memory usage and bandwidth requirements significantly, especially for integrated graphics cards, but can cause z-fighting with some resource packs due to how it reduces the precision of position and texture coordinate attributes.
sodium.options.use_fog_occlusion.name=Use Fog Occlusion
sodium.options.use_fog_occlusion.tooltip=If enabled, chunks which are determined to be fully hidden by fog effects will not be rendered, helping to improve performance. The improvement can be more dramatic when fog effects are heavier (such as while underwater), but it may cause undesirable visual artifacts between the sky and fog in some scenarios.
sodium.options.use_entity_culling.name=Use Entity Culling
sodium.options.use_entity_culling.tooltip=If enabled, entities determined not to be in any visible chunks will be skipped during rendering. This can help improve performance by avoiding the rendering of entities located underground or behind walls.
sodium.options.use_particle_culling.name=Use Particle Culling
sodium.options.use_particle_culling.tooltip=If enabled, only particles which are determined to be visible will be rendered. This can provide a significant improvement to frame rates when many particles are nearby.
sodium.options.animate_only_visible_textures.name=Animate Only Visible Textures
sodium.options.animate_only_visible_textures.tooltip=If enabled, only animated textures determined to be visible will be updated. This can provide a significant boost to frame rates on some hardware, especially with heavier resource packs. If you experience issues with some textures not being animated, try disabling this option.
sodium.options.translucency_sorting.name=Translucency Sorting
sodium.options.translucency_sorting.tooltip=If enabled, translucent blocks will be sorted correctly from back to front to provide better rendering, especially when multiple translucent blocks are in view and layered.  This is a bit of an expensive operation.
sodium.options.cpu_render_ahead_limit.name=CPU Render-Ahead Limit
sodium.options.cpu_render_ahead_limit.tooltip=Specifies the maximum number of frames the CPU can be waiting on the GPU to finish rendering. Very low or high values may create frame rate instability.
sodium.options.cpu_render_ahead_limit.value=%s frame(s)
sodium.options.allow_direct_memory_access.name=Allow Direct Memory Access
sodium.options.allow_direct_memory_access.tooltip=If enabled, some critical code paths will be allowed to use direct memory access for performance. This often greatly reduces CPU overhead for chunk and entity rendering, but can make it harder to diagnose some bugs and crashes. You should only disable this if you've been asked to or otherwise know what you're doing.
sodium.options.ignore_driver_blacklist.name=Ignore Driver Blacklist
sodium.options.ignore_driver_blacklist.tooltip=If enabled, known incompatibilities with your hardware/driver configuration will be ignored, allowing you to enable options that may cause issues with your game. You should generally not touch this option unless you know exactly what you are doing. After changing this option, you must save, close, and then re-open the settings screen.
sodium.options.enable_memory_tracing.name=Enable Memory Tracing
sodium.options.enable_memory_tracing.tooltip=Debugging feature. If enabled, stack traces will be collected alongside memory allocations to help improve diagnostic information when memory leaks are detected.
sodium.options.performance_impact_string=Performance Impact: %s
sodium.options.use_persistent_mapping.name=Use Persistent Mapping
sodium.options.use_persistent_mapping.tooltip=If enabled, a small amount of memory will be persistently mapped for speeding up chunk updates and entity rendering.\n\nRequires OpenGL 4.4 or ARB_buffer_storage.
sodium.options.chunk_memory_allocator.name=Chunk Memory Allocator
sodium.options.chunk_memory_allocator.tooltip=Selects the memory allocator that will be used for chunk rendering.\n- ASYNC: Fastest option, works well with most modern graphics drivers.\n- SWAP: Fallback option for older graphics drivers. May increase memory usage significantly.
sodium.options.chunk_memory_allocator.async=Async
sodium.options.chunk_memory_allocator.swap=Swap
sodium.options.chunk_update_threads.name=Chunk Update Threads
sodium.options.chunk_update_threads.tooltip=Specifies the number of threads to use for chunk building. Using more threads can speed up chunk loading and update speed, but may negatively impact frame times.
sodium.options.always_defer_chunk_updates.name=Always Defer Chunk Updates
sodium.options.always_defer_chunk_updates.tooltip=If enabled, rendering will never wait for chunk updates to finish, even if they are important. This can greatly improve frame rates in some scenarios, but it may create significant visual lag in the world.
sodium.options.use_no_error_context.name=Use No Error Context
sodium.options.use_no_error_context.tooltip=If enabled, the OpenGL context will be created with error checking disabled. This may slightly improve performance, but it also increases the risk that the game will crash instead of gracefully handling OpenGL errors. You should disable this option if you are experiencing sudden unexplained crashes.
sodium.options.threads.value=%s thread(s)
sodium.options.default=Default
sodium.options.buttons.undo=Undo
sodium.options.buttons.apply=Apply
sodium.options.buttons.donate=Buy coffee for JellySquid!
yumelium.options.pages.plus=Yumelium Plus
yumelium.options.render_sky.name=Render Sky
yumelium.options.render_sky.tooltip=If disabled, the sky (gradient, sun, moon and stars) will not be rendered, leaving a void-black sky. Can improve frame rates.
yumelium.options.render_weather.name=Render Weather
yumelium.options.render_weather.tooltip=If disabled, rain and snow will not be rendered. This can improve frame rates and visibility during storms.
yumelium.options.render_fog.name=Render Fog
yumelium.options.render_fog.tooltip=If disabled, distance fog will not be rendered, improving visibility. May look unusual at the edge of the render distance.
yumelium.options.screen_shake.name=Screen Shake
yumelium.options.screen_shake.tooltip=If disabled, the camera will not tilt/shake when you take damage.
yumelium.options.better_grass.name=Better Grass
yumelium.options.better_grass.tooltip=Renders the grass texture on the sides of grass/mycelium/podzol/snow blocks so the ground looks continuous.\n- Fast: all visible side faces.\n- Fancy: only where the block continues (adjacent or one step down).\nReloads chunks when changed.
yumelium.options.dynamic_lights.name=Dynamic Lights
yumelium.options.dynamic_lights.tooltip=Held or dropped light-emitting items (torches, glowstone, ...) and burning entities cast light on the world around them.\n- Fast: updated every few ticks (fewer chunk rebuilds).\n- Fancy: updated every tick (smoothest, more rebuilds).
yumelium.options.dynamic_lights_shaders.name=Dynamic Lights + Shaders
yumelium.options.dynamic_lights_shaders.tooltip=Run dynamic lights even while a shader pack is active. Off by default: packs like Complementary cast their own (colored) handheld light, and running both doubles the light and pays the chunk re-mesh cost. Enable for packs without handheld lighting.
yumelium.options.debug_logging.name=Debug Logging
yumelium.options.mod_renderer_cache.name=Mod Renderer Caching
yumelium.options.mod_renderer_cache.tooltip=Caches the geometry of expensive procedural mod renderers (Betweenlands Sludge Menace body). The shadow pass build is reused by the camera pass, and distant bodies update at a reduced rate; nearby animation is unchanged.
yumelium.options.debug_logging.tooltip=Verbose diagnostic logging: shader pack rosters, capability probe details, pipeline notes, block-id mapping reports. Off keeps the log to verdict lines and warnings only.
yumelium.options.zoom_enabled.name=Zoom
yumelium.options.zoom_enabled.tooltip=Enables the hold-to-zoom key (assign it under Controls → Yumelium).
yumelium.options.zoom_smooth.name=Smooth Zoom
yumelium.options.zoom_smooth.tooltip=If enabled, zooming in/out animates smoothly instead of snapping.
yumelium.options.zoom_scroll.name=Zoom Scrolling
yumelium.options.zoom_scroll.tooltip=If enabled, scrolling the mouse wheel while zoomed adjusts the zoom depth (and won't switch hotbar slots).
yumelium.options.zoom_reduce_sensitivity.name=Reduce Sensitivity
yumelium.options.zoom_reduce_sensitivity.tooltip=If enabled, mouse look sensitivity is lowered in proportion to the zoom depth, so a deeper zoom aims more finely.
yumelium.options.connected_textures.name=Connected Textures
yumelium.options.connected_textures.tooltip=Connected textures (currently: glass). Requires the Yumelium companion resource pack, which supplies the tiles (the mod does not ship them). With no such pack installed, glass renders normally.
yumelium.options.pages.nvidium=Nvidium
yumelium.options.nvidium_enabled.name=Nvidium Renderer
yumelium.options.nvidium_enabled.tooltip=NVIDIA mesh-shader terrain renderer. When on (and supported by your GPU), terrain is drawn entirely by GPU mesh shaders with occlusion culling for maximum performance. Requires an RTX/mesh-shader-capable NVIDIA GPU; has no effect otherwise. Changing this reloads the renderer.
yumelium.options.nvidium_buffer_size.name=Nvidium Buffer Size
yumelium.options.nvidium_buffer_size.tooltip=Maximum VRAM budget for Nvidium's GPU-resident terrain geometry. The buffer starts small and grows on demand up to this cap. Raise it for very high render distances if distant chunks stop drawing; lower it to save VRAM. Unlimited caps at your GPU's total dedicated VRAM (queried from the driver). Changing this reloads the renderer.
yumelium.options.nvidium_buffer_size.512mb=512 MB
yumelium.options.nvidium_buffer_size.1gb=1 GB
yumelium.options.nvidium_buffer_size.2gb=2 GB
yumelium.options.nvidium_buffer_size.4gb=4 GB
yumelium.options.nvidium_buffer_size.unlimited=Unlimited (GPU VRAM)
yumelium.options.nvidium_translucent_sort.name=Translucent Sorting
yumelium.options.nvidium_translucent_sort.tooltip=How Nvidium orders translucent geometry (water/glass) for correct blending.\n- Off: unsorted (fastest, may mis-blend overlapping transparency).\n- Section: sort visible sections back-to-front (default, fixes the common cases).\n- Full: Section plus per-quad sorting within each section (most correct, extra cost). Every visible translucent quad is re-sorted on the CPU while the camera moves — very expensive in water-heavy worlds (e.g. The Betweenlands swamp); prefer Section there.
yumelium.options.nvidium_translucent_sort.off=Off
yumelium.options.nvidium_translucent_sort.section=Section
yumelium.options.nvidium_translucent_sort.full=Full
yumelium.options.nvidium_gpu_culling.name=GPU Culling
yumelium.options.nvidium_gpu_culling.tooltip=Culls terrain sections on the GPU in a task shader before any vertex work runs. Falls back automatically when the task stage is unavailable.
yumelium.options.nvidium_occlusion_culling.name=Occlusion Culling
yumelium.options.nvidium_occlusion_culling.tooltip=Additionally skips sections the depth buffer proved hidden behind other terrain — the big win in hilly or heavily wooded views. Requires GPU Culling. May briefly pop when spinning the camera.
yumelium.options.multidraw_mode.name=Multi Draw Mode
yumelium.options.multidraw_mode.tooltip=How chunk sections are submitted to the GPU (all use Vertex Array Objects).\n- Direct: one glMultiDrawElementsBaseVertex per region (default, good balance).\n- Individual: one draw call per section (most compatible, highest CPU cost).\n- Indirect: glMultiDrawElementsIndirect per region (GL 4.3; lowest driver overhead; falls back to Direct if unsupported).
yumelium.options.multidraw_mode.indirect=Indirect
yumelium.options.multidraw_mode.individual=Individual
yumelium.options.multidraw_mode.direct=Direct
yumelium.options.pages.extra=Yumelium Extra
yumelium.options.render_sun_moon.name=Render Sun & Moon
yumelium.options.render_sun_moon.tooltip=If disabled, the sun and moon will not be rendered.
yumelium.options.render_stars.name=Render Stars
yumelium.options.render_stars.tooltip=If disabled, stars will not be rendered at night.
yumelium.options.render_sky_colors.name=Sky Colors
yumelium.options.render_sky_colors.tooltip=If disabled, the sky uses a fixed neutral color instead of the biome/time-based sky color.
yumelium.options.render_particles.name=All Particles
yumelium.options.render_particles.tooltip=Master switch for particles. If disabled, no particles (smoke, splashes, etc.) are rendered. Can improve frame rates in particle-heavy scenes.
yumelium.options.particle_rain_splash.name=Rain Splash
yumelium.options.particle_rain_splash.tooltip=If disabled, the small splash particles from falling rain are not spawned. The rain ambience sound is kept.
yumelium.options.particle_block_break.name=Block Break
yumelium.options.particle_block_break.tooltip=If disabled, the burst of particles when a block is fully broken is not spawned.
yumelium.options.particle_block_breaking.name=Block Breaking
yumelium.options.particle_block_breaking.tooltip=If disabled, the small particles that fly off while a block is being mined are not spawned.
yumelium.options.animate_block_textures.name=All Animations
yumelium.options.animate_block_textures.tooltip=Master switch for texture animations. If disabled, all animated textures are frozen. This can reduce GPU load, especially with high-resolution resource packs.
yumelium.options.animate_water.name=Water Animation
yumelium.options.animate_water.tooltip=If disabled, the water texture stops animating (still shown, but frozen).
yumelium.options.animate_lava.name=Lava Animation
yumelium.options.animate_lava.tooltip=If disabled, the lava texture stops animating.
yumelium.options.animate_fire.name=Fire Animation
yumelium.options.animate_fire.tooltip=If disabled, the fire texture stops animating.
yumelium.options.animate_portal.name=Portal Animation
yumelium.options.animate_portal.tooltip=If disabled, the nether portal texture stops animating.
yumelium.options.animate_other.name=Other Animations
yumelium.options.animate_other.tooltip=If disabled, all other animated block textures (sea lantern, magma, prismarine, ...) stop animating.
yumelium.options.biome_colors.name=Biome Colors
yumelium.options.biome_colors.tooltip=If disabled, grass, foliage and water use a fixed default color instead of per-biome colors. Reloads chunks when changed.
yumelium.options.show_fps.name=Show FPS
yumelium.options.show_fps.tooltip=Displays the current frame rate in the top-left corner of the screen.
yumelium.options.show_coordinates.name=Show Coordinates
yumelium.options.show_coordinates.tooltip=Displays your current X/Y/Z position in the top-left corner of the screen.
yumelium.options.hud_position.name=HUD Position
yumelium.options.hud_position.tooltip=Which screen corner the FPS/coordinates HUD is drawn in.
yumelium.options.hud_position.top_left=Top Left
yumelium.options.hud_position.top_right=Top Right
yumelium.options.hud_position.bottom_left=Bottom Left
yumelium.options.hud_position.bottom_right=Bottom Right
yumelium.options.hud_shadow.name=HUD Text Shadow
yumelium.options.hud_shadow.tooltip=If enabled, the FPS/coordinates HUD text is drawn with a drop shadow for readability.
yumelium.options.shader_health_report.name=Shader Health Report
yumelium.options.shader_health_report.tooltip=Logs one full report of everything the shader engine skips, does not implement, or failed at (program routing, pack directives, compile failures, sampler audits) after the next frame. Toggle off and on to print it again. Log-only.
